            <ArticleTitle>Probing the Atomic Structure of Transient Protein Contacts by Paramagnetic Relaxation Enhancement Solution NMR.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>243-255</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/978-1-4939-7386-6_12</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Important biological processes, including enzyme catalysis, signaling, and protein folding, proceed through lowly populated (&lt;5%) states that elude structural characterization by conventional techniques. Here, we describe the steps required for visualization of these sparsely populated conformations and transient protein-protein interactions using paramagnetic relaxation enhancement solution NMR. We describe experimental design, sample preparation, data acquisition and processing, and the basics of data analysis of structural ensembles.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
